# WHERE THIS GOES depends on what you put in it.
#
#   the API KEY  ->  ~/.config/autosound/critic-env     (Windows: %APPDATA%\autosound\critic-env)
#   everything else -> rew_analitic/.critic-env in the project, if you want it per-car
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/autosound && cp scripts/.critic-env.example ~/.config/autosound/critic-env
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/autosound/critic-env
#
# And do NOT `export GEMINI_API_KEY` from ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc. A file is read by whoever knows
# its path; an exported variable is handed to EVERY process you start -- every npm package, every
# agent, every `env`. The wrappers export it themselves for the length of their own run, which is
# as long as it needs to exist.
#
# The key stays out of the project because the project folder is the one the README suggests
# backing up to a private GitHub. Both files are read, the machine one first, so an existing
# project-local file keeps working exactly as before.
#
# READ as KEY=VALUE, never executed: a line containing $( , a backtick or ; is dropped with a
# message. Quotes around a value are optional and stripped; they cost nothing and read clearer.

# ---- Default: real Antigravity (agy) ----
GEMINI_BIN=agy
# Critic = Pro, Advisor = Flash. These were the other way round in this file until 2026-08-12,
# which handed anyone who copied it the rubber-stamp reviewer the docs spend paragraphs warning
# about ("a Flash critic praises"). The reviewer is the role that must NOT agree with you; the
# advisor answers routine questions, where Flash is the right trade.
# Slug ids, as `agy models` prints them in its LEFT column: the display labels this file carried
# ("Gemini 3.1 Pro (High)") are rejected by agy >= 1.1.12 with "invalid model selection".
GEMINI_CRITIC_MODEL=gemini-3.1-pro-high
GEMINI_ADVISOR_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-medium

# ---- Fallback: @google/gemini-cli via an API KEY (cross-platform) ----
# gemini-cli's OWN sign-in is CLOSED (2026-09-08, IneligibleTierError: "This client is no longer
# supported for Gemini Code Assist for individuals … migrate to the Antigravity suite") — the
# binary works with a key ONLY. Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — the current
# shape is AQ.… (53 chars); an AIza… (39) key is the old shape and answers API_KEY_INVALID once a
# new one exists. Keep the key in THIS file (per machine), not in a shell export: a session's
# environment does not follow ~/.zshrc after it started.
# GEMINI_BIN=gemini
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AQ....                       # exported to gemini-cli automatically
# GEMINI_CRITIC_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro           # API ids for this CLI; Critic = Pro
# GEMINI_ADVISOR_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# PROJECT_MIRROR=/abs/path/to/project/rew_analitic   # only if CWD differs from the project
